---
name: "Solutions"
title: "Sickle cell, thalassaemia and SMA tests | Lightening Lives"
description: "LitLife™ tests from a dried blood spot for sickle cell, beta and alpha thalassaemia and SMA, for hospitals, labs and public health. New tests on request."
label: Solutions
kicker: "Institutional diagnostic solutions"
h1: 'Five ready-to-run LitLife™ kits. <span class="h-mark">Custom tests built on request.</span>'
lead: "Molecular tests for inherited blood and muscle disorders that work directly from a dried blood spot, for hospitals, lab chains, CSR initiatives and public health programmes."
proof:
  - { icon: "badge-check", text: "ICMR approved" }
  - { icon: "award", text: "Patents granted in India and Japan" }
  - { icon: "map-pin", text: "15 sites, 9 states and Delhi" }
openingWide: true
notice: true
closing:
  h2: 'Start with the condition <span class="h-mark">your programme needs.</span>'
  body: "Tell us who will be tested, roughly how many, and where. Our scientific and operations team replies with a technical and commercial approach."
  solid: { text: "Talk to our scientific team", enquire: true }
  line: { text: "Partner with us", href: "/partner-with-us/" }
---
{#- Solutions (content file 5.3), since 25 October 2026 the user's catalogue grid, grouped by family;
    since the client review (5 November 2026, plan Task 4) each kit a clear card that opens (P2:
    "replace 'Drag to Turn' product boxes with clear expandable cards"): its box as a picture, its
    condition, its name (β and α, P1), the points that matter on the card and Details for the rest,
    with "Read more" to its test page and "Request product sheet"; DMD and LGMD as cards that ask our
    scientific team; under development (the client's order: the pipeline, then co-development);
    Develop a test with us (#develop); and Beyond the kits, four things we bring, without buttons. The kits come from src/site/_data/kits.json. The jump links under
    the opening are the page's navigation. -#}
{%- set arrow = '<svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="12" viewBox="0 0 18 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M1 6h15M11 1l5 5-5 5"/></svg>' %}
{%- from "picture.njk" import picture with context %}
{%- from "faq.njk" import faq %}

  <!-- The kits we have, standing together: the page's navigation, each box to its card -->
  <section id="kits" class="section kit-lineup" aria-labelledby="kits-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="kits-h" class="sr-only">The kits, by family</h2>
      <div class="lineup">
        {%- for family in kits.families %}
        <div class="lineup-family" style="--n: {{ family.kits.length }}">
          <p class="lineup-family-h"><span>{{ family.name }}</span></p>
          <ul class="lineup-kits">
            {%- for kit in family.kits %}
            <li>
              <a class="lineup-kit" href="#{{ kit.id }}">
                <span class="lineup-box">{{ picture("box-lineup-" + kit.model.kit, "", "(min-width: 64rem) 17vw, 40vw", { class: "lineup-img" }) }}</span>
                <span class="lineup-name">{{ kit.name | replace("LitLife™-", "") }}</span>
                <span class="lineup-condition">{{ kit.title }}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="lineup-foot">
        <ul class="kit-shared">
          <li>{% icon "droplet" %}<span>A dried blood spot</span></li>
          <li>{% icon "thermometer" %}<span>Room temperature transport</span></li>
          <li>{% icon "flask-conical" %}<span>No DNA extraction</span></li>
          <li>{% icon "microscope" %}<span>Standard PCR equipment</span></li>
        </ul>
        <ul class="lineup-more">
          <li><a class="link" href="#in-development">Under development {{ arrow | safe }}</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="#develop">Develop a test with us {{ arrow | safe }}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- for family in kits.families %}
  <!-- {{ family.name }} -->
  <section id="{{ family.id }}" class="section{{ ' bg-paper' if loop.first }}" aria-labelledby="{{ family.id }}-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="{{ family.id }}-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7"><span class="family-icon icon-tile">{% icon family.icon %}</span>{{ family.name }}. <span class="h-mark">{{ family.sub }}.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">{{ family.lead }}</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="kit-grid mt-12">
        {%- for kit in family.kits %}
        {#- A datasheet card (the user, 5 November 2026: "the details etc can be included in the card
            without clicking"): the box; the condition, the name and the proof as a seal; every
            point; then the two ways on, along the foot. -#}
        {%- set points = [] %}
        {%- for f in kit.features.concat(kit.more) %}{% if f != "ICMR approved" %}{% set points = (points.push(f), points) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        {%- set proof = "ICMR approved" in kit.features %}
        <li id="{{ kit.id }}" class="kit-card kit-sheet">
          <div class="kit-shot">
            {{ picture(kit.image, kit.alt, "(min-width: 72rem) 18vw, (min-width: 40rem) 45vw, 92vw", { class: "kit-img" }) }}
          </div>
          <div class="kit-body">
            <div class="kit-head">
              <span class="kit-condition">{{ kit.title }}</span>
              <h3 class="kit-name" id="{{ kit.id }}-name">{{ kit.name }}</h3>
              {%- if proof %}
              <p class="kit-proof"><span class="cred-mark cred-seal">{% icon "badge-check" %}</span>ICMR approved</p>
              {%- endif %}
            </div>
            <ul class="kit-points">
              {%- for f in points %}
              <li>{% icon "circle-check-big" %}<span>{{ f }}</span></li>
              {%- endfor %}
            </ul>
            <p class="kit-acts">
              <a class="kit-act kit-act-main" href="{{ kit.href }}">Read more {% icon "arrow-right" %}</a>
              <a class="kit-act" {{ { condition: kit.enquire, topic: "dossier" } | enquire | safe }}>{% icon "file-text" %}Request product sheet</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- if family.ask and family.ask.length %}
        <li class="kit-asks">
          {%- for ask in family.ask %}
          {%- set askSlug = { dmd: "duchenne-muscular-dystrophy", lgmd: "limb-girdle-muscular-dystrophy" }[ask.id] %}
          <div id="{{ ask.id }}" class="kit-card kit-ask">
            <a class="kit-link" {{ { condition: askSlug } | enquire | safe }}>
              <span class="kit-body">
                <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "message-circle" %}</span>
                <span class="kit-condition">Molecular diagnosis available</span>
                <span class="kit-name">{{ ask.condition }}</span>
                <span class="kit-line">{{ ask.line | unbracket }}</span>
                <span class="kit-more">Talk to our scientific team {% icon "arrow-right" %}</span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </div>
          {%- endfor %}
        </li>
        {%- endif %}
      </ul>
      {%- if family.also %}
      <p class="kit-also">{% icon "plus" %}<span>{{ family.also.text }} <span class="kit-also-links">{% for l in family.also.links %}<a class="link" href="{{ l.href }}">{{ l.text }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</span></span></p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

  <!-- Under development: the kits to come, drawn as outlines beside the kits we have -->
  <section id="in-development" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="in-development-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="in-development-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Under development. <span class="h-mark">Expanding accessible precision medicine.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Want early access for your hospital or laboratory, or to join multi-centre clinical validation? Tell us.</p>
      </div>
      {%- set ghost %}<svg class="ghost-box" viewBox="0 0 240 170" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path class="ghost-floor" d="M24 138 L120 162 L216 138 L120 118 Z"/><path class="ghost-edge" d="M40 52 L120 72 L200 52 L120 34 Z M40 52 L40 126 L120 148 L120 72 M200 52 L200 126 L120 148"/></svg>{% endset %}
      <ul class="next-kits mt-12">
        {%- for item in [
          { icon: "droplets", name: "Blood coagulation panel", body: "Genetic testing for inherited bleeding disorders, including haemophilia A and B, to confirm a clinical diagnosis, identify carriers and support family counselling." },
          { icon: "pill", name: "Pharmacogenomics panel", body: "Testing for the genetic variations that decide how a patient responds to key medicines, so clinicians can choose the right drug and dose and avoid adverse reactions." }
        ] %}
        <li class="next-kit">
          <div class="next-stage">
            {{ ghost | safe }}
            <span class="next-mark">{% icon item.icon %}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="next-body">
            <span class="next-tag">{% icon "hourglass" %}Under development</span>
            <h3>{{ item.name }}</h3>
            <p>{{ item.body }}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      <div class="next-act">
        <a class="btn btn-line" {{ { topic: "early-access" } | enquire | safe }}>Partner with us for early access</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Develop a test with us: the page's main ask -->
  <section id="develop" class="section" aria-labelledby="develop-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="develop">
        <div class="develop-ask">
          <h2 id="develop-h" class="h2">Develop a test with us. <span class="h-mark">Propose a condition.</span></h2>
          <p class="lead mt-5">Every LitLife™ kit began with a programme's need. If your hospital, lab chain or state health mission needs a test that doesn't exist, our scientists can develop and validate it.</p>
          <p class="develop-when-h">It makes sense when you have</p>
          <ul class="develop-when">
            <li>{% icon "users" %}<span>A condition common in one community or region</span></li>
            <li>{% icon "map-pin" %}<span>A regional mutation no test covers</span></li>
            <li>{% icon "package" %}<span>A dried blood spot format no manufacturer offers</span></li>
          </ul>
          <div class="develop-act">
            <a class="btn btn-solid" {{ { topic: "develop" } | enquire | safe }}>Propose a condition</a>
            <a class="link" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Develop%20a%20test">Write to our R&amp;D team {{ arrow | safe }}</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="develop-path">
          {%- set steps = [
            { icon: "message-circle", title: "Brief", body: "You tell us the condition, the population and the setting." },
            { icon: "search", title: "Feasibility", body: "Our scientists assess the genetics and the method." },
            { icon: "dna", title: "Development", body: "We design and optimise the test." },
            { icon: "clipboard-check", title: "Validation", body: "We validate it against reference methods on real samples." },
            { icon: "graduation-cap", title: "Rollout", body: "Training, supply and support for your programme." }
          ] %}
          {%- for step in steps %}
          <li>
            <span class="develop-node">{% icon step.icon %}</span>
            <div>
              <h3><span class="develop-n">{{ loop.index }}</span>{{ step.title }}</h3>
              <p>{{ step.body }}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beyond the kits: four things we bring to a programme (P2: no buttons) -->
  <section id="beyond" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="beyond-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="beyond-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Beyond the kits. <span class="h-mark">What we bring to a programme.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">The clinical, nutritional, operational and training support a programme needs, in public health, CSR, hospital and laboratory settings.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="beyond mt-12">
        <li><div><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "users" %}</span><b>Testing and nutrition programmes</b><span>End-to-end screening for patients, carriers and newborns, custom community panels, and nutritional assessment.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "megaphone" %}</span><b>Awareness and genetic counselling</b><span>Community awareness drives, dried blood spot screening camps, prenatal diagnosis guidance and genetic counselling for carrier families.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "graduation-cap" %}</span><b>Hands-on technical training</b><span>Workshops and certification for laboratory technicians and health workers, so every laboratory runs the test the same way.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "microscope" %}</span><b>Lab set-up and grant consultancy</b><span>Setting up cost-effective district or hospital molecular laboratories, and technical planning for government and CSR proposals.</span></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Questions we are asked -->
  <section id="faq" class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
    <div class="wrap grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      <h2 id="faq-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-5">Questions <span class="h-mark">we are asked.</span></h2>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        {{ faq([
          { q: "Do you test individuals?", a: "No. We work with hospitals, laboratories, clinicians, NGOs, CSR funders and government health programmes. If you are looking for a test for yourself or your family, please speak to your doctor or visit your nearest government health facility." },
          { q: "What does our laboratory need to run the kits?", a: "A thermal cycler, a gel electrophoresis tank and a punch, a bench, and staff who have run PCR or have been trained. No proprietary system. We help set the method up and train your staff." },
          { q: "How do samples reach the laboratory?", a: "On the card, at room temperature, by ordinary courier or post. No cold chain." },
          { q: "Are the kits approved?", a: "LitLife™-SCA, our sickle cell kit, is approved by ICMR, which validated it with 100% sensitivity and specificity. The technology behind our kits is patented in India and Japan." },
          { q: "How quickly are results ready?", a: "The same day. Many cards run together, and screening and confirmation come from the same run." },
          { q: "Can you develop a test for a condition that isn't listed?", a: "Yes. Each test we have developed began with an institution that needed it. Tell us the condition and the setting, and we take it from there." }
        ]) }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
